[32m+[m[32m**Average (Moyenne)** compares the target with an alpha-weighted linear-light[m
[32m+[m[32mmean. Pixels with alpha ≤ 10 are excluded; remaining sRGB pixels are converted to[m
[32m+[m[32mlinear RGB before averaging and converted back afterward. This avoids averaging[m
[32m+[m[32mgamma-encoded values directly. The database also retains a naive sRGB mean for[m
[32m+[m[32mcomparison.[m
 [m
[31m----[m
[32m+[m[32m**Dominant (Dominante)** uses deterministic weighted k-means in OKLab, with up to[m
[32m+[m[32mfive clusters. Border pixels receive less clustering weight. The representative[m
[32m+[m[32mis an actual pixel nearest the strongest cluster's center; the dominant ratio[m
[32m+[m[32muses alpha weights without the border adjustment.[m
